11. HashSet Internal Working (🔥 4+ Years Topic)
Uses HashMap internally
Elements stored as keys

Uses:
hashCode()
equals()

👉 If both match, element is considered duplicate.

12. Custom Object in HashSet (🔥 VERY IMPORTANT)
Employee Class
class Employee {
    int id;
    String name;

    Employee(int id, String name) {
        this.id = id;
        this.name = name;
    }

    @Override
    public int hashCode() {
        return id;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object obj) {
        Employee e = (Employee) obj;
        return this.id == e.id;
    }
}

Test Class
import java.util.*;

public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Set<Employee> set = new HashSet<>();

        set.add(new Employee(1, "Sai"));
        set.add(new Employee(1, "Sai"));
        set.add(new Employee(2, "Ram"));

        System.out.println(set.size());
    }
}

Output
2
👉 Without overriding equals() & hashCode(), duplicates will not be removed ❗


